{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both tests pass. The fix in `repo/stats.py`:\n\n```python\ns = sorted(values)\nn = len(s)\nmid = n // 2\nif n % 2:\n    return s[mid]\nreturn (s[mid - 1] + s[mid]) / 2\n```\n\nThe bug: for even-count columns the old code returned `s[mid - 1]` (the lower-middle element) instead of averaging the two middle values. That's why medians looked wrong on some columns — odd-length columns were fine, but even-length columns were reporting the lower-middle value. Now even-length lists correctly return the average of the two middle values (e.g. `median([1, 2, 3, 4]) == 2.5`)."}]},"session_id":"cf631ec1-5f80-4e7e-8376-3ebf2c94cf28"}
